[thin] Functional internal tube stop. The nominal Ø5.00 throat leaves 0.475 mm of axial TPU and 0.675 mm radial overlap beneath the Ø6.35 factory tail. Its 45° entry taper retains 0.50 mm nominal clearance to the actual Ø6.05 chamfered pump tip. The current native slice has five closed circumferential roads on each of four stop layers, with no wet support. This is a compliant wet fitting feature, outside the nominal 3 mm PET-GF structural-wall rule; the ranked thickness remains applicable. Physical stop bearing, insertion force and life are unqualified.
alternatives: A 3 mm axial stop in the same 15 mm body shortens one of the two 6 mm sealing lands or changes the installed package. A smaller throat lengthens the retained 45° taper and reduces its axial rim. Removing the stop loses the factory-tail insertion datum. These alternatives require another receiver design and application qualification.
