[thin] Functional fold-through front lip. The Ø14 mm funnel lip is 0.60 mm axially so it can deform through the closed Ø12 mm wall opening during factory assembly. The wall and rear keeper then retain the receiver. This named TPU flexure is intentionally thinner than an ordinary rigid wall; printed folding, sealing and retention remain unqualified.
alternatives: A rigid 3 mm lip changes the required folding profile and insertion behavior. Splitting the wall or adding a separate front retainer changes the closed-wall assembly. Removing the lip loses the continuous entry funnel and its front capture.
