[thin] Functional compliant mounting collar. The Ø17.5 mm collar has a 1.10 mm axial peripheral rim at Y5.9..7.0 and a 51.58° exterior ramp at Y3.6..5.9. The matched wall retains a full 3 mm PET-GF neck behind the 0.6 mm front recess. The actual native slice has nine complete circumferential roads on each of nine rim layers; every sampled ramp layer has a closed road and backed outermost-road centerline. The ranked TPU thickness remains applicable. These command paths establish neither holding strength nor layer adhesion.
alternatives: A thicker rim in the same axial package requires a steeper mounting ramp while retaining the wall neck and Y7 keeper datum; it changes the compliant collar and support contacts. A longer package moves the keeper, factory socket and tee interface. Removing the rim removes positive capture. None is an ordinary rigid-stock thickening of this wet part.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-pump-receiver.step
click: x=1.317 y=5.680 z=8.369
click: x=1.317 y=7.000 z=8.369

[thin] Functional compliant funnel and socket wall. The source specifies Ø11.70 outside and Ø6.10 sealing bores, giving 2.80 mm radial cuffs. The funnel grows from the 6.10 mm sealing land to a Ø9 entry; its reported oblique section and the ramp-to-cuff section are parts of that continuous flexible profile. The relaxed outside fits the Ø12 wall and rear-support bores with 0.15 mm radial room. The manually fitted TPU elbow supports the initial bore choice only; this double receiver has no physical fit, pressure or endurance acceptance.
alternatives: A 3 mm radial cuff at the same bore requires Ø12.10 outside, exceeding the present Ø12 wall/frame openings. Enlarging those openings and revising the keeper neck changes the assembly. Reducing the entry funnel changes its misalignment capture; reducing the seal bore increases nominal interference. Those are application changes requiring a receiver fit and retention result.
